rubrics_metrics.description:
TeX assigns demerits to lines and seeks sequence of breakpoints that minimizes total demerits. For a line with badness b and associated penalty p, demerits d are:
- (l + b)^2 + p^2 if 0 ≤ p < 10000;
- (l + b)^2 − p^2 if −10000 < p < 0;
- (l + b)^2 if p ≤ −10000.
Here l is \linepenalty (plain TeX sets \linepenalty=10).
